    "workflow": "Decision and Structuring",
    "full_prompt": "The source materials provided for this request follow.\n\nEntity: Salesforce, Inc.\nCASH FLOW (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2022-01-31 | FY end 2023-01-31 | FY end 2024-01-31 | FY end 2025-01-31 | FY end 2026-01-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities | 6,000,000,000 | 7,111,000,000 | 10,234,000,000 | 13,092,000,000 | 14,996,000,000\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInInvestingActivities | -14,536,000,000 | -1,989,000,000 | -1,327,000,000 | -3,163,000,000 | -8,590,000,000\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInFinancingActivities | 7,838,000,000 | -3,562,000,000 | -7,477,000,000 | -9,429,000,000 | -8,079,000,000\nPaymentsToAcquirePropertyPlantAndEquipment | 717,000,000 | 798,000,000 | 736,000,000 | 658,000,000 | 594,000,000\n\n---\n\nEntity: Salesforce, Inc.\nBALANCE SHEET (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2022-01-31 | FY end 2023-01-31 | FY end 2024-01-31 | FY end 2025-01-31 | FY end 2026-01-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nAssets | 95,209,000,000 | 98,849,000,000 | 99,823,000,000 | 102,928,000,000 | 112,305,000,000\nLiabilities | 37,078,000,000 | 40,490,000,000 | 40,177,000,000 | 41,755,000,000 | 53,163,000,000\nStockholdersEquity | 58,131,000,000 | 58,359,000,000 | 59,646,000,000 | 61,173,000,000 | 59,142,000,000\nAssetsCurrent | 22,850,000,000 | 26,395,000,000 | 29,074,000,000 | 29,727,000,000 | 28,222,000,000\nLiabilitiesCurrent | 21,788,000,000 | 25,891,000,000 | 26,631,000,000 | 27,980,000,000 | 37,118,000,000\nCashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue | 5,464,000,000 | 7,016,000,000 | 8,472,000,000 | 8,848,000,000 | 7,327,000,000\nAccountsReceivableNetCurrent | 9,739,000,000 | 10,755,000,000 | 11,414,000,000 | 11,945,000,000 | 14,339,000,000\nLongTermDebtNoncurrent | 10,592,000,000 | 9,419,000,000 | 8,427,000,000 | 8,433,000,000 | 10,439,000,000\nLongTermDebt | 10,596,000,000 | 10,601,000,000 | 9,426,000,000 | 8,433,000,000 | 14,439,000,000\n\nUsing these materials, complete the following request.\n\nProduce a scenario comparison decision brief for Salesforce, Inc. covering the four fiscal-year scenarios FY2023 through FY2026 using only the supplied annual 10-K balance-sheet and cash-flow materials. Begin with a one-sentence statement of the strongest cash-generation scenario among the four fiscal years. Structure the brief as exactly four scenario columns, one for each fiscal year from FY2023 through FY2026. In each column, compute free cash flow as NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities minus PaymentsToAcquirePropertyPlantAndEquipment, showing both inputs and the result in whole USD and preserving the reported signs, concepts, and fiscal endpoints exactly as they appear in the materials; do not round, relabel, or convert any source figure. Independently verify the FY2026 total assets figure of 112,305,000,000 against the sum of reported Liabilities and StockholdersEquity for the same fiscal endpoint, and state whether it ties out. Reconcile the FY2026 CashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue of 7,327,000,000 against the same-period AssetsCurrent and LiabilitiesCurrent, and identify any mismatch between the reported cash position and the current-asset composition as Unresolved. For every derived metric, variance, and tie-out conclusion, identify the supporting balance-sheet or cash-flow concept and the exact reported figure used, keeping the source label beside each input. Apply the fiscal endpoints 2023-01-31 through 2026-01-31 consistently as the scenario periods, and verify that every balance-sheet and cash-flow input used in the comparison is drawn from the same fiscal endpoint. Show each derived metric with two decimal places where applicable while keeping underlying source values in whole USD. Close with a one-sentence evidence gap statement identifying any reported balance-sheet or cash-flow input still needed to confirm the cross-statement tie-out. If any derived comparison or tie-out cannot be established from the supplied materials, label it Not Determinable.",
    "response_model": "Qwen3.5-27B",
    "response": "### Scenario Comparison Decision Brief: Salesforce, Inc. (FY2023–FY2026)\n\n**Strongest Cash-Generation Scenario:** The FY end 2026-01-31 scenario represents the strongest cash-generation period with a Free Cash Flow of $14,402,000,000, derived from the highest reported NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities of $14,996,000,000 and the lowest PaymentsToAcquirePropertyPlantAndEquipment of $594,000,000 among the four years.\n\n| Metric / Concept | FY end 2023-01-31 | FY end 2024-01-31 | FY end 2025-01-31 | FY end 2026-01-31 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Free Cash Flow Calculation** | | | | |\n| *Input:* NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities | 7,111,000,000 | 10,234,000,000 | 13,092,000,000 | 14,996,000,000 |\n| *Input:* PaymentsToAcquirePropertyPlantAndEquipment | 798,000,000 | 736,000,000 | 658,000,000 | 594,000,000 |\n| **Derived:** Free Cash Flow (Operating - CapEx) | 6,313,000,000.00 | 9,498,000,000.00 | 12,434,000,000.00 | 14,402,000,000.00 |\n| **Balance Sheet Tie-Out Verification** | | | | |\n| *Input:* Assets | 98,849,000,000 | 99,823,000,000 | 102,928,000,000 | 112,305,000,000 |\n| *Input:* Liabilities | 40,490,000,000 | 40,177,000,000 | 41,755,000,000 | 53,163,000,000 |\n| *Input:* StockholdersEquity | 58,359,000,000 | 59,646,000,000 | 61,173,000,000 | 59,142,000,000 |\n| *Calculation:* Sum of Liabilities + Equity | 98,849,000,000.00 | 99,823,000,000.00 | 102,928,000,000.00 | 112,305,000,000.00 |\n| **Tie-Out Conclusion (FY2026)** | N/A | N/A | N/A | **Ties Out** (Assets 112,305,000,000 = Liabilities 53,163,000,000 + Equity 59,142,000,000) |\n| **Cash Position Reconciliation (FY2026)** | | | | |\n| *Input:* CashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue | 7,016,000,000 | 8,472,000,000 | 8,848,000,000 | 7,327,000,000 |\n| *Input:* AssetsCurrent | 26,395,000,000 | 29,074,000,000 | 29,727,000,000 | 28,222,000,000 |\n| *Input:* LiabilitiesCurrent | 25,891,000,000 | 26,631,000,000 | 27,980,000,000 | 37,118,000,000 |\n| **Reconciliation Status (FY2026)** | N/A | N/A | N/A | **Unresolved**: Reported Cash (7,327,000,000) is less than AssetsCurrent (28,222,000,000); specific composition of non-cash current assets is not provided to verify the remainder. |\n\n**Evidence Gap Statement:** To fully confirm the cross-statement tie-out for the FY2026 cash position reconciliation, the specific breakdown of non-cash components within AssetsCurrent (such as AccountsReceivableNetCurrent, Inventory, or Prepaid Expenses) is required to mathematically validate that the sum of these components plus CashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue equals the total AssetsCurrent figure.",
