    "full_prompt": "The source materials provided for this request follow.\n\nEntity: THE BOEING COMPANY\nBALANCE SHEET (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2021-12-31 | FY end 2022-12-31 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-31 | FY end 2025-12-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nAssets | 138,552,000,000 | 137,100,000,000 | 137,012,000,000 | 156,363,000,000 | 168,235,000,000\nLiabilities | 153,398,000,000 | 152,948,000,000 | 154,240,000,000 | 160,277,000,000 | 162,778,000,000\nStockholdersEquity | -14,999,000,000 | -15,883,000,000 | -17,233,000,000 | -3,908,000,000 | 5,454,000,000\nAssetsCurrent | 108,666,000,000 | 109,523,000,000 | 109,275,000,000 | 127,998,000,000 | 128,459,000,000\nLiabilitiesCurrent | 81,992,000,000 | 90,052,000,000 | 95,827,000,000 | 97,078,000,000 | 108,115,000,000\nCashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue | 8,052,000,000 | 14,614,000,000 | 12,691,000,000 | 13,801,000,000 | 10,921,000,000\nAccountsReceivableNetCurrent | 2,641,000,000 | 2,517,000,000 | 2,649,000,000 | 2,631,000,000 | 2,921,000,000\nLongTermDebt | 57,921,000,000 | 56,794,000,000 | 52,055,000,000 | 53,625,000,000 | 53,848,000,000\nOtherLiabilitiesNoncurrent | 1,750,000,000 | 2,211,000,000 | 2,332,000,000 | 2,318,000,000 | 2,432,000,000\n\n---\n\nEntity: THE BOEING COMPANY\nCASH FLOW (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2021-12-31 | FY end 2022-12-31 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-31 | FY end 2025-12-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities | -3,416,000,000 | 3,512,000,000 | 5,960,000,000 | -12,080,000,000 | 1,065,000,000\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInInvestingActivities | 9,324,000,000 | 4,370,000,000 | -2,437,000,000 | -11,973,000,000 | 499,000,000\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInFinancingActivities | -5,600,000,000 | -1,266,000,000 | -5,487,000,000 | 25,209,000,000 | -3,763,000,000\nPaymentsToAcquirePropertyPlantAndEquipment | 980,000,000 | 1,222,000,000 | 1,527,000,000 | 2,230,000,000 | 2,942,000,000\n\nUsing these materials, complete the following request.\n\nPrepare a BA balance sheet position reported balance sheet facts extraction brief — evidence-integrated revision for THE BOEING COMPANY, written for a credit-review analyst performing due diligence. Use a neutral, evidence-bound tone and define each statement concept on first use without editorializing on the company's condition.\n\nUse only the supplied annual balance sheet and cash flow materials for fiscal years ending 2021-12-31 through 2025-12-31. Preserve all reported amounts, signs, fiscal year-end dates, concept labels, and units exactly as shown. Keep negative values such as StockholdersEquity and NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities unaltered, and do not round any source value before completing a calculation or comparison. Apply the fiscal year-end dates 2021-12-31 through 2025-12-31 consistently to every balance sheet and cash flow figure, and state that all comparisons are aligned to the same annual reporting endpoints.\n\nFor each fiscal year 2021 through 2025, calculate the balance sheet identity check as Assets minus Liabilities minus StockholdersEquity, using the reported annual figures from the balance sheet material, and present the resulting residual in USD. Independently verify the reported NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities for each fiscal year by checking that the sign and magnitude shown in the cash flow material are internally consistent with the disclosed concept label and reporting year, and state whether each year ties out or retains an unexplained variance. For every reported figure, calculation, and cross-statement observation, identify the source material, statement type, concept label, and fiscal year, and keep the source label beside each numeric input and result.\n\nLabel any requested figure or comparison that cannot be established from the supplied materials as Not Determinable rather than estimating or importing outside data. Close the brief with a Next action line that states the single most material unresolved reporting observation from the five-year comparison and the specific figure requiring follow-up.",
