    "full_prompt": "The source materials provided for this request follow.\n\nEntity: THE BOEING COMPANY\nINCOME STATEMENT (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2021-12-31 | FY end 2022-12-31 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-31 | FY end 2025-12-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nRevenues | 62,286,000,000 | 66,608,000,000 | 77,794,000,000 | 66,517,000,000 | 89,463,000,000\nCostOfRevenue | 59,237,000,000 | 63,078,000,000 | 70,070,000,000 | 68,508,000,000 | 85,174,000,000\nGrossProfit | 3,049,000,000 | 3,530,000,000 | 7,724,000,000 | -1,991,000,000 | 4,289,000,000\nOperatingIncomeLoss | -2,870,000,000 | -3,519,000,000 | -773,000,000 | -10,707,000,000 | 4,281,000,000\nNetIncomeLoss | -4,202,000,000 | -4,935,000,000 | -2,222,000,000 | -11,817,000,000 | 2,235,000,000\nIncomeTaxExpenseBenefit | -743,000,000 | 31,000,000 | 237,000,000 | -381,000,000 | 397,000,000\nResearchAndDevelopmentExpense | 2,249,000,000 | 2,852,000,000 | 3,377,000,000 | 3,812,000,000 | 3,615,000,000\nEarningsPerShareBasic (USD/shares) | -7.15 | -8.3 | -3.67 | -18.36 | 2.49\n\n---\n\nEntity: THE BOEING COMPANY\nBALANCE SHEET (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2021-12-31 | FY end 2022-12-31 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-31 | FY end 2025-12-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nAssets | 138,552,000,000 | 137,100,000,000 | 137,012,000,000 | 156,363,000,000 | 168,235,000,000\nLiabilities | 153,398,000,000 | 152,948,000,000 | 154,240,000,000 | 160,277,000,000 | 162,778,000,000\nStockholdersEquity | -14,999,000,000 | -15,883,000,000 | -17,233,000,000 | -3,908,000,000 | 5,454,000,000\nAssetsCurrent | 108,666,000,000 | 109,523,000,000 | 109,275,000,000 | 127,998,000,000 | 128,459,000,000\nLiabilitiesCurrent | 81,992,000,000 | 90,052,000,000 | 95,827,000,000 | 97,078,000,000 | 108,115,000,000\nCashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue | 8,052,000,000 | 14,614,000,000 | 12,691,000,000 | 13,801,000,000 | 10,921,000,000\nAccountsReceivableNetCurrent | 2,641,000,000 | 2,517,000,000 | 2,649,000,000 | 2,631,000,000 | 2,921,000,000\nLongTermDebt | 57,921,000,000 | 56,794,000,000 | 52,055,000,000 | 53,625,000,000 | 53,848,000,000\nOtherLiabilitiesNoncurrent | 1,750,000,000 | 2,211,000,000 | 2,332,000,000 | 2,318,000,000 | 2,432,000,000\n\n---\n\nEntity: THE BOEING COMPANY\nCASH FLOW (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2021-12-31 | FY end 2022-12-31 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-31 | FY end 2025-12-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities | -3,416,000,000 | 3,512,000,000 | 5,960,000,000 | -12,080,000,000 | 1,065,000,000\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInInvestingActivities | 9,324,000,000 | 4,370,000,000 | -2,437,000,000 | -11,973,000,000 | 499,000,000\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInFinancingActivities | -5,600,000,000 | -1,266,000,000 | -5,487,000,000 | 25,209,000,000 | -3,763,000,000\nPaymentsToAcquirePropertyPlantAndEquipment | 980,000,000 | 1,222,000,000 | 1,527,000,000 | 2,230,000,000 | 2,942,000,000\n\nUsing these materials, complete the following request.\n\nPrepare a cross-statement reported-facts extract for The Boeing Company using only the three supplied annual 10-K extracts. I want to assess whether the strongest year-on-year earnings improvement in this series was accompanied by stronger cash generation, liquidity and equity, without inferring business causes from selected statement lines.\n\nFirst, calculate the signed dollar change in NetIncomeLoss for each adjacent-year comparison from FY end 2021-12-31 through FY end 2025-12-31. Show those comparisons and select the fiscal year with the largest positive dollar change—not a percentage growth rate from a loss base. Use that selected year and its immediate predecessor as the focal pair for the rest of the analysis.\n\nBuild a compact, side-by-side extract of every reported input used below. Identify each input’s source statement, exact reported concept name and fiscal endpoint. Express monetary amounts in USD millions, preserving signs and exact converted values; distinguish annual income and cash-flow amounts from year-end balance-sheet balances. Label calculations as derived, and do not treat an absent line as zero.\n\nFor both focal years, calculate and compare:\n- Operating margin, defined here as OperatingIncomeLoss divided by Revenues; show its change in percentage points.\n- Operating cash flow minus NetIncomeLoss, retaining the sign of the difference rather than turning it into an absolute gap.\n- Operating cash flow after PP&E acquisition payments, defined here as NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities minus PaymentsToAcquirePropertyPlantAndEquipment. Treat this as an analyst-defined measure, not a reported company metric.\n- Net working capital, defined as AssetsCurrent minus LiabilitiesCurrent.\n\nAlso show the dollar changes in reported operating cash flow, CashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue and StockholdersEquity. Use unrounded inputs throughout and display margins to two decimal places.\n\nPerform two limited consistency checks. For each focal year, calculate Assets minus Liabilities minus StockholdersEquity. For the selected year only, calculate the change in CashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue from the predecessor’s year-end balance, sum that selected year’s reported operating, investing and financing cash flows using their reported signs, and calculate the residual as the cash-balance change minus that cash-flow sum. Show the substitutions and signed residuals. Call a zero residual an exact arithmetic match; describe a nonzero amount as a residual, not automatically a reporting error. Do not present either check as a complete reconciliation or invent an omitted component to close it.\n\nEnd with a concise assessment driven by these results. Evaluate cash generation using both operating cash flow and the after-PP&E measure, liquidity using both cash and net working capital, and equity using reported StockholdersEquity. Distinguish improvement from a positive ending level, and call the evidence mixed if indicators within a dimension move in opposing directions. Explain whether these dimensions support the same conclusion as the selected earnings rebound. For each nonzero consistency residual, separate the measurable difference from its undetermined explanation and propose a targeted follow-up disclosure request as analyst judgment, not as a document requirement established by the extracts.",
